data.broker-url-and-login-app#Broker URL and:
Two Actions variables supply the broker URL and the login app client ID, not the repository:
Variable Container environment AGENT_TOKEN_BROKER_URL TOKEN_BROKER_URL AGENT_LOGIN_CLIENT_ID LOGIN_APP_CLIENT_ID A repository variable of the same name overrides the organization value. Nothing in the container can read variables, so broker-env.sh runs on the host as initializeCommand. It needs gh (logged in, repo scope) and jq, reads both variables for the origin repository and writes .devcontainer/.env, which runArgs passes with --env-file:
{ "initializeCommand": ".devcontainer/broker-env.sh", "runArgs": ["--env-file=${localWorkspaceFolder}/.devcontainer/.env"] }
